# CR 903.10a, 707.2: a copy of a commander is not a commander, so the combat damage it deals is no commander damage.
# Bot1's commander, Raging Goblin (haste), deals Bot2 1 combat damage on turn 1. On turn 2 Bot2's Clone enters as a copy
# of it - a Raging Goblin with haste - and attacks Bot1 for 1: Bot1 loses the life, but no commander dealt it.
# Fixture only: Raging Goblin stands in for a commander; the harness does not check commander eligibility.

[Format]
Commander

[Bot1 Commander]
Raging Goblin

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain x25

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Clone
Island x22

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Command.Raging Goblin.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Raging Goblin > Bot2)
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Clone.Cast
Bot2.Accept
? Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Raging Goblin
Bot2.Attack(Raging Goblin > Bot1)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Bot1.Life = 39
Bot2.Life = 39
Bot1.Commander.Raging Goblin.DamageTo.Bot1 = 0
Bot1.Commander.Raging Goblin.DamageTo.Bot2 = 1
